rting. Report as \'k of n\', and state the small sample and virtual-contract-only limits. Do not claim user validation before the confirmation round.\n\nThe 80%/90% thresholds, the 3-person repeat rule and the 12-person confirmation round are my proposed values, with no basis elsewhere in the repo. The decision is made by the agent on the owner\'s behalf, and the owner can override it before the test starts.\n\n**Why:** The repo fixes the criteria (5s, 30s, 2 taps, misunderstanding rate) in CONSUMER_FLOW_SPEC §7, 화면 설계서 §12-6, 제3부 §51.5 and Masterplan v0.3, and says 8–12 people is for problem discovery, not proof. It sets no pass numbers, so release gate 9 cannot be judged. Axis 4 of the implementation plan forbids reporting \'이해됨\' without thresholds fixed beforehand. U6 is added because the 시안 비교 comparison and T-AP-07 depend on consumers not reading \'확인 필요\' as a computed amount or as \'no coverage\'. With 12 participants, 90% means at most one misunderstanding. The thresholds are a minimum bar before launch, not statistical proof. The test has not been run, so nothing here says the screens are understood.\n\n**Options:** [\'A (chosen): six tasks, round 1 of 8–12 for problem discovery plus a confirmation round of 12 or more, thresholds frozen in PREREG before the test\', "B: five tasks and a single 8–12 person round that decides pass/fail. This drops the \'computed vs 확인 필요\' task and reports \'이해됨\' from a tiny sample", \'C: large statistically powered sample of dozens to hundreds. This is too costly for a pre-launch virtual-contract test and out of proportion to its purpose\', \'D: set the thresholds after seeing results. This is forbidden by implementation plan axis 4 and amounts to fitting the criteria to the outcome\']\n\n**Revisit if:** The owner changes the thresholds or sample size; round 1 shows a task was badly designed; the target user group changes; an external review or regulator asks for a larger sample; or the screen flow changes so the task wordi